{"problem_sha256":"eef5a1f83bb66d5156d89eceaee6f6dbc225d8de799acbd8424421bffb19003b","input_sha256":"452b66e86bf77f95ba287d23676b86f25e8039d813955fef42fea6a892ff5f38","read_receipts":[],"usage":{"provider_requests":null,"total_tokens":null},"output":{"briefing":"This slot concerns only the explicit family dkp_square_family, not a proof that it exhausts Diophantine sextuples. Its target is: for every rational t not in {0,1,-1}, all six listed coordinates are nonintegers. Write d=t^2-1, h=t^2+1, v=t^4+34t^2+1. The exact coordinates are a=-9h/(8d), b=(t^2-7)h(7t^2-1)/(8d^3), c=8d^3/(9h^3), e=-2(t^2+5)(5t^2+1)/(9dh), f=-2t(t^2-4t-3)(3t^2-4t-1)(t^3+8t^2+5t+4)(4t^3-5t^2+8t-1)/(dhv^2), and g=2t(t^2+4t-3)(3t^2+4t-1)(t^3-8t^2+5t-4)(4t^3+5t^2+8t+1)/(dhv^2). For this domain, put t=m/n in lowest terms with n>0: m≠0 and m^2≠n^2. The denominators are nonzero. The source function itself permits t=0 (where f=g=0), but that parameter is explicitly excluded from the auxiliary claim.

The suggested route is not established evidence. A simple check worth proving explicitly is |c|=(8/9)|d/h|<8/9, since |t^2-1|<t^2+1; thus c is nonzero and nonintegral on the target domain. For the other coordinates, derive divisibility and valuation conditions from reduced m,n rather than assuming denominators survive cancellation. In particular, the proposal suggests negative 2-adic valuations for a,b and that integrality of e may force H|32, with H=m^2+n^2 and D=m^2-n^2; prove all such claims including odd/even cases and cancellation. For f,g, set Q=m^4+34m^2n^2+n^4. If using polynomial gcd/Bezout arguments against q(T)=T^4+34T^2+1, derive exact identities or certificates; the proposal's resultant figures are unverified hints, not lemmas. It suggests possible Q support only at 2 and 3, followed by exact v2(Q), v3(Q) analysis and comparison with Q>36. Prove each implication and handle factors that vanish, signs, and all exceptional cases. Check the t↦−t relation between f and g explicitly; do not infer that one coordinate's nonintegrality automatically settles the other without proving the relation's exact effect. A contradiction-style argument via necessary divisibility/local conditions is a possible distinct method, but method choice remains with the prover.

Return either a complete all-height proof for this family claim, or the strongest partial theorem whose proof is complete and correctly quantified; clearly label any remaining family cases. Finite searches do not establish the unbounded claim. Even a complete family exclusion would not resolve the locked problem: existence/nonexistence for unrestricted signs and for all-positive sets remains open, and the family has not been shown exhaustive. Do not promote prior experiments or the proposal to accepted results; no reusable lemmas, reviews, or selected attempts are recorded.","uncertainties":["The all-height nonintegrality claim for the six-coordinate family remains unproved; in particular the necessary valuation/divisibility implications, Bezout certificates, Q support and local valuation cases, and f/g exceptional or cancellation cases require proof.","The proposal's suggested resultant values are not independently verified and must not be used as established identities.","The family claim, whether proved or refuted, does not by itself settle either the unrestricted-sign or all-positive main existence question."],"problem_contract":{"acceptance_profile":"reviewed","assumptions":["All six elements are nonzero rational numbers and pairwise distinct.","At least two elements are integers.","Each of the fifteen pairwise products plus one is a rational square; zero square roots are allowed."],"objective":"proof","quantifiers":["Existentially over all six-element rational sets, with no bound on rational height or integer anchors.","A nonexistence argument must cover every allowable set and every integer-anchor pair."],"source_refs":[],"statement":"Determine whether there exists a set of six pairwise distinct nonzero rational numbers containing at least two integers, with xy+1 a rational square for every distinct pair. Track the all-positive and unrestricted-sign cases separately. Auxiliary construction-family exclusions are partial results and do not decide the main question."},"selected_attempt_ids":[],"selected_review_ids":[],"emphasis_tags":["explicit-family-only","all-height","reduced-parameter","cancellation","bezout-certificates","2-adic-cases","3-adic-cases","f-g-symmetry","do-not-conflate-main-goal"],"selected_lemma_ids":[],"artifact_reading_list":["family_core.txt (full text; exact dkp_square_family definition; SHA-256 cec9e6858695754bae9f3147a9dd6028aa46aae5b5194bcae44b5845d9bf81e3)","proposal.md (full text; unproved continuation proposal and suggested route; SHA-256 99e3e54dee87a6cec71fe1fb4e652b483f9f3c817a2241fbbb3f70dddbcf9482)"],"diversity_constraints":{"avoid_methods":[],"preferred_method_family":"contradiction","must_differ_from_prior_attempts":true}}}
